    {
        "content": "<p>Is <code>linter.docPrime</code> even still enabled?</p>",
        "id": 623177258,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1789052169
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>My thought is to rename (all) conjugation by inverse lemmas to <code>inv_{right, left}_conjugate</code> to match the conjugation by star lemmas (example, <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=star_left_conjugate_pos#doc\">docs#star_left_conjugate_pos</a>, <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=star_right_conjugate_pos#doc\">docs#star_right_conjugate_pos</a>, etc).</p>",
        "id": 623178883,
        "sender_full_name": "Monica Omar",
        "timestamp": 1789052467
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Note that <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=ConjAct#doc\">docs#ConjAct</a> , <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=MulAut.conj#doc\">docs#MulAut.conj</a> uses the shorter spelling</p>",
        "id": 623180958,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1789052943
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>We usually default to putting the inverses at the end: <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=IsConj#doc\">docs#IsConj</a>, <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=MulAut.conj_apply#doc\">docs#MulAut.conj_apply</a>, <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=commutatorElement_def#doc\">docs#commutatorElement_def</a></p>\n<p>The prime naming is also used for <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Subgroup.mem_normalizer_iff%27%27#doc\">docs#Subgroup.mem_normalizer_iff''</a></p>",
        "id": 623183549,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1789053494
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Matrix.trace_units_conj#doc\">docs#Matrix.trace_units_conj</a> already has the inverse at the end, right?</p>",
